<title>USA: U.S Ex-Im bank approves loans for China projects.</title>
<headline>U.S Ex-Im bank approves loans for China projects.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Export-Import Bank of the United States Tuesday approved about $792 million in direct loans to support the export of U.S. equipment and services for two power projects in China.</p>
<p>Ex-Im said its board authorized a $408.8 million loan supporting the sale by Foster Wheeler Corp of six coal-fired boilers for the Yangcheng Power Plant in China's Shanxi Province.</p>
<p>The board also approved a $383 million loan supporting the sale of plant equipment and services for the Qinshan III power plant by  Bechtel Corp.</p>
</text>
